heretek-onboarding-classes-passive-abilities-title = Passive abilities

heretek-class-soldier-name = Soldier
heretek-class-soldier-description = A specialist in reliable ranged combat and the use of long-range weapons.
heretek-class-soldier-lore-note = A Soldier is valued not for solitary glory but for the discipline of the firing line: take position, hold the sector, and deny the enemy its preferred range.
heretek-class-soldier-navigation-description = Accurate fire and support.
heretek-class-soldier-active-ability = Run and Gun — a future manoeuvre for changing position and immediately firing at a priority target.
heretek-class-soldier-passive-ability = Steady Aim — holding position will improve the accuracy of ranged weapons.

heretek-class-assassin-name = Assassin
heretek-class-assassin-description = A hunter of isolated targets who relies on stealth and a sudden strike.
heretek-class-assassin-lore-note = An Assassin reads the battlefield as a map of vulnerabilities: choose an isolated target, strike precisely, and vanish before the enemy can rally.
heretek-class-assassin-navigation-description = Stealth and sudden strikes.
heretek-class-assassin-active-ability = Seek the Opening — a future manoeuvre that marks a vulnerable point on a target for the next precise attack.
heretek-class-assassin-passive-ability = Lone Killer — operating away from allies will improve evasion and escape from enemy pressure.

heretek-class-overseer-name = Overseer
heretek-class-overseer-description = A summoner who will eventually support themselves through subordinate creatures.
heretek-class-overseer-lore-note = An Overseer keeps retainers and subordinates in formation by voice, signal, and constant control; their strength lies in the right order at the right moment.
heretek-class-overseer-navigation-description = Commanding summons.
heretek-class-overseer-active-ability = Command the Subordinate — a future order directing a summoned creature to a target, position, or task.
heretek-class-overseer-passive-ability = Overseer's Link — subordinates will answer commands more quickly and protect their commander.

heretek-class-warrior-name = Warrior
heretek-class-warrior-description = A melee combatant who holds the front line and accepts danger personally.
heretek-class-warrior-lore-note = A Warrior takes the first blow so others do not have to. Heavy armour, discipline, and resolve turn the front line into a line that holds.
heretek-class-warrior-navigation-description = Front line and defense.
heretek-class-warrior-active-ability = Endure — a future defensive technique that briefly strengthens resilience before a decisive clash.
heretek-class-warrior-passive-ability = Interception — a successful defense will create an opening to answer enemy pressure at once.

heretek-class-operative-name = Operative
heretek-class-operative-description = A specialist in electronic systems and supporting allies.
heretek-class-operative-lore-note = An Operative wins through preparation: breaches systems, spots weak points, and turns intelligence on the enemy into an advantage for the entire squad.
heretek-class-operative-navigation-description = Hacking and support.
heretek-class-operative-active-ability = Analyze Enemy — a future manoeuvre that exposes a target's weakness and prepares it for a coordinated attack.
heretek-class-operative-passive-ability = Calculated Shot — precise single shots from a favourable position will gain additional effectiveness.

